234 722 239 722 250C722 261 715 266 707 270L409 270L409 568C405 576 399 583 389 583C379 583 374 575 370 570L369 420L369 270L70 270C62 266 56 261 56 250Z\"></path><path id=\"MJX-TEX-N-34\" d=\"M462 0L471 0L471 46L442 46C401 47 392 48 385 54C379 60 379 59 379 114L379 165L471 165L471 211L379 211L379 671L373 677L355 677C338 677 336 677 334 675C332 674 274 586 179 442L28 211L28 165L287 165L287 115C287 81 287 63 286 61C284 57 279 52 274 51C266 48 253 47 221 46L190 46L190 0L199 0C213 3 306 3 333 3C359 3 448 3 462 0M293 211L183 211L74 212L293 545Z\"></path></defs></svg>","mathFallback":false,"description":"JEE Main's 2014 JEE Main 2014 (Offline) Paper's All Questions with solutions provider ExamSIDE.Com","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2014 (Offline)","nextq":"wHLdpNBwztknpOVP","prevq":"jIFtaNeZrGrvSnIr","questions":[{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","question_id":"OW5Yew1POHLRleED","exam":"jee-main","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"subjectGroup":null,"subject":"chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","languages":["en"],"chapter":"compounds-containing-nitrogen","year":2014,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2014 (Offline)","difficulty":"medium","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":null,"question":{"en":{"content":"Considering the basic strength of amines in aqueous solution, which one has the smallest pK<sub>b</sub> value?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"(CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>N"},{"identifier":"B","content":"C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>NH<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"(CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>NH"},{"identifier":"D","content":"CH<sub>3</sub>NH<sub>2</sub>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Arylamines are less basic than alkyl amines and even ammonia. This is due to resonance. In aryl amines the lone pair of electrons on <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.009ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 888 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is partly shared with the ring and is thus less available for sharing with a portion.\n<br><br>In alkylamines, the electron releasing alkyl group increases the electron density on nitrogen atom and thus also increases the ability of amine for protonation. Hence more the no. of alkyl groups higher should be the basicity of amine. But a slight discrepancy occurs in case of trimethyl amines due to steric effect. Hence the correct order is \n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\" display=\"true\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.646ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"50.069ex\" height=\"2.342ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 22130.3 1035.4\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(389,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(760,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1648,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2473.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-