roke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 2LiCl + K<sub>2</sub>O </p>\n<p>The above equation is incorrect because K<sub>2</sub>O, a stronger base cannot be generated by a weaker base, Li<sub>2</sub>O.</p>\n<p>(D) [CoCl(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>5</sub>]<sup>+</sup> + 5H<sup>+</sup> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Co<sup>2+</sup> + <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.69ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.701ex\" height=\"2.554ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 2962 1128.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\" transform=\"translate(1388,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(973.9,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-305.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> + Cl<sup>-</sup></p>\n<p>The above equation is correct because amine complexes decomposes under acidic medium. Thus, the complex [CoCl(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>5</sub>] decomposes under acidic conditions to give ammonium ions.</p>"}},"permalink":"the-equation-which-is-balanced-and-represents-the-correct-pr-2014-marks-4-fl6mtawicj141ojv.htm","timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"jee-main-2014-offline","topic":"coordination-number","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2014-offline","active":true}],"ids":["OW5Yew1POHLRleED","QKjkxVH5bPaZitm7","bCoAkDQsvbeCdFkG","Fl6mTAWICJ141OJv"],"title":"JEE Main 2014 (Offline) | JEE Main Year Wise Previous Years Questions","canonical":"https://app/past-years/jee/considering-the-basic-strength-of-amines-in-aqueous-solution-2014-marks-4-ow5yew1pohlrleed.htm"}